  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 857.379310px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": [
    "All nine selected single originals were actually inspected at native size on light and dark mattes. Two ossicones, two pink inner ears, intact orange reticulated patches, white oval eye surrounds, cream muzzle, two connected hoof-ended arms, two feet and one tufted tail retain clear boundaries without extra appendages or visible alpha background clouds.",
    "All five maximum-use both-matte pages were actually viewed at inherited body-reference857.379310px. The head/ossicone/eye outlines, patch gaps, tail connection and hoof divisions remain readable, with no visibly smeared or clipped ends. Paper grain stays inside clean major shape boundaries.",
    "Neutral-blink-neutral keeps the quiet head/body/feet proportions near the adopted usual; it does not replace a subtle blink with a global body stretch. Greet and left/right gestures use the corresponding hoof arm and gaze. Think uses a tilted head and chin hoof; aha opens the mouth; cheer raises two attached arms without introducing fingers.",
    "All seven decoded recipe rows were actually viewed. Species A lowers/turns the ears with a small head/neck attention dip and B returns toward upright; these are deliberate active pose changes rather than a quiet-blink rescale. Grounded feet stay aligned in the discrete neighbors."
  ],
  "cautions": [
    "The hand-drawn reticulated patch boundaries and ossicone spacing have small pose-to-pose differences; active species head/ear attention changes are more visible than idle blink, and should still be checked in final timing.",
    "The result accepts static native/max-use stock and discrete recipe neighbors; no real-time playback, physical UI pixel-density measurement or compressed completed MP4 is claimed."
  ],
